ent-MedievalAlchemyGuide = alchemy parchment
    .desc = A parchment explaining how to extract aspects and brew potions.
alchemy-guide-basics-aspects = Alchemy involves extracting aspects, mixing them in the required proportions, and performing a series of alchemical operations on them to produce a potion. Extracting aspects: an alchemist can examine an alchemical ingredient to learn which aspects it yields when dissolved and which solvent it requires. To extract aspects from an ingredient, grind it in a mortar, then pour the resulting liquid into a suitable vessel and heat it until ready. The more aspects an ingredient yields, the more solvent it requires.
alchemy-guide-basics-potions = Brewing potions: to brew a potion, you need to know its recipe. Tier 1 recipes are fixed, while more complex recipes can be found in alchemical recipe scrolls scattered around the world or sold by a merchant. Measure the aspects listed in the recipe in the required proportions; multiply every ingredient by the same factor for larger batches. Combine all ingredients before the first step and perform the operations strictly in order. Stirring requires a spoon, a campfire is suitable for heating, and the remaining operations require specialized stations. These can be found in the alchemist's house, crafted by artisans, or purchased from a merchant. Many alchemical stations require both a vessel containing the necessary aspects as input and a vessel in the output slot to collect the result.
